.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt DISKUTIL 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm diskutil
.Nd disks, partitions and volumes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list Op Ar disk
.Nm
.Cm info Oo Fl plist Oc Ar disk | mountPoint
.Nm
.Cm mount Oo Cm readOnly Oc Oo Fl mountPoint Ar path Oc Ar disk
.Nm
.Cm mountDisk Ar disk
.Nm
.Cm unmount Oo Cm force Oc Ar disk | mountPoint
.Nm
.Cm unmountDisk Oo Cm force Oc Ar disk
.Nm
.Cm eject Ar disk
.Nm
.Cm rename Ar disk name
.Nm
.Cm verifyVolume | repairVolume Ar disk | mountPoint
.Nm
.Cm eraseVolume Ar format name disk
.Nm
.Cm listFilesystems
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
works on the disks
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8
knows: it asks it to mount, unmount, eject and rename them, and shows how
it describes each.
A
.Ar disk
is named as
.Pa disk2s1 ,
.Pa /dev/disk2s1
or by the mount point of its volume.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm list
Every disk and its partitions, with their type, volume name, size and
identifier; or those of one disk.
.It Cm info
A disk's or volume's description; with
.Fl plist ,
as a property list.
.It Cm mount , Cm mountDisk
Mounts a volume (in
.Pa /Volumes ,
or at
.Ar path ) ,
or every volume of a disk.
.It Cm unmount , Cm unmountDisk
Unmounts a volume, or every volume of a disk;
.Cm force
even when files are open on it.
.It Cm eject
Unmounts the volumes of a disk and ejects it.
.It Cm rename
Renames a volume.
.It Cm verifyVolume , Cm repairVolume
Checks a volume's file system with its
.Nm fsck_ Ns Ar type ,
or repairs it (unmounted for the time it takes).
A mounted HFS Plus volume is verified as it is.
.It Cm eraseVolume
Makes a new file system on a volume, with its
.Nm newfs_ Ns Ar type ,
and mounts it.
.It Cm listFilesystems
The formats
.Cm eraseVolume
takes: JHFS+, HFS+, JHFSX, HFSX, FAT32, FAT16, FAT12 and MS-DOS.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl diskutil list
.Dl diskutil info /
.Dl diskutil eraseVolume FAT32 USB disk2s1
.Dl diskutil eject disk2
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hdiutil 1 ,
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8 ,
.Xr fsck_hfs 8 ,
.Xr fsck_msdos 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr newfs_hfs 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
.Sh HISTORY
This
.Nm
was written for Minkar, after macOS's.
It has no partitioning, APFS or RAID verbs yet.
